### Benchmark working data lives at repo-root data/ (see "Data & checkpoints" above)

# The bare `data/` pattern above is meant for the repo-root working data, but
# it matches every directory of that name -- including the pipeline's own
# sources, which then never reach a node and fail there as "no such file".
!scripts/plant2_ft_pipeline/data/

### nuPlan statistics that ship with the benchmark
# `*.json` (line 25) and `*.csv` (line 65) above are blanket rules for working
# output. They also swallowed the statistics the benchmark itself depends on:
# density_calibration_sumo.json is read at run time by
# traffic_bench/eval/engine/traffic/traffic_density_levels.py, so an ignored copy
# means a fresh clone raises FileNotFoundError on the first expanded scene.
# The csv are stored gzipped (46 MB instead of 113 MB); pandas reads .csv.gz
# directly, so nothing downstream has to be told about it.
!traffic_bench/eval/engine/traffic/nuplan_statistics/*.json
!tools/nuplan_resample/stats_r150/*.json
